WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.030
This is a true story of a four-legged hero as well as animal friendship and care.
这是一个真实的故事，讲述了一位四条腿的英雄以及动物之间的友谊和关爱。

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.690
Everything took place in Nairobi, Kenya—a country in East Africa.
这一切都发生在东非国家肯尼亚的内罗毕。

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:16.800
When she was just a few weeks old, a small elephant sadly lost her mother to a poacher attack.
一头小象才几周大的时候，就不幸在一次盗猎袭击中失去了妈妈。

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.900
Luckily, the little elephant was found by a farmer and taken to an elephant orphanage where she was named Natumi.
幸运的是，这头小象被一位农民发现，送到了一所大象孤儿院，并在那里被取名为纳图米。

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:30.210
There, at the David Sheldrick Wildlife Trust, Natumi was safe, but very scared and shy.
在那里，也就是在大卫·谢尔德里克野生动物基金会，纳图米很安全，但非常害怕，也很害羞。

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.580
Soon, however, new orphaned baby elephants began to arrive at the shelter.
然而没过多久，新的小象孤儿开始陆续来到收容所。

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:44.460
At first, Natumi hid behind her keeper’s legs, but it soon became clear that the other baby elephants needed someone to depend on.
起初，纳图米躲在饲养员的腿后面，但大家很快就看出来，其他小象需要有个依靠。

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:49.400
They were very young and many of them had injuries like wounds and scratches.
它们年纪都很小，其中许多身上带着伤口、擦伤之类的外伤。

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.050
To everyone’s surprise, shy little Natumi stepped up to the task.
令所有人惊讶的是，害羞的小纳图米挺身而出，承担起了这项任务。

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:01.760
She began to act like a big sister to the seven other elephants, keeping them calm and playing with them in the surrounding bush.
她开始像大姐姐一样对待另外七头象，让它们保持平静，还在周边的荒野里陪它们玩耍。

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.690
Guided by Natumi, the elephants had soon formed their own loving family.
在纳图米的带领下，这些小象很快就组成了自己的家庭，彼此相亲相爱。

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:18.550
In the end, the new family of elephants was strong and healthy enough to return to the wild—but the workers at the shelter would never forget a little elephant named Natumi who made it possible.
最后，这个新的大象家庭已经足够强壮、健康，可以回归野外了，但收容所的工作人员永远不会忘记那头名叫纳图米的小象——是她让这一切成为可能。
